WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.035 size:78% position:39%
-Welcome to the show!

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.370
-Thank you.
Thank you for finally having me.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, and I´m sorry it took me
this long to have you,

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also want to apologize
for something else.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What´s that?

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your co-stars,
Lili and Camila, right?

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They came on the show,
Betty and Veronica,

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was excited
to talk to them

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
about some of their co-stars
on the show --

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
Luke Perry, Molly Ringwald,
big deals to me,

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
being the age I am.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.721
And we had this exchange,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you´ll understand
why I owe you an apology.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you found out
you were working with them,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
did those names
mean anything to you?

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
I mean, everyone -- Yeah.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.898
-They meant -- Yeah, I mean, I
didn´t know who Luke Perry was.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.367 size:75% position:38%
-For me, it was more
like Cole Sprouse.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, for us, it was like,
"Cole Sprouse?"

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Suite Life,"
we grew up with that.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Now, tell me something
real quick.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.241 size:75% position:38%
Who is Cole Sprouse?

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m so sorry.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.413
But it would have been slightly
creepy if I knew who you were.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whatever helps you
get to sleep at night.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I am so -- I apologize.
-No, please, come on.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:55.622
-But, you know, I wasn´t
watching a lot of Disney Channel

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my late 20s.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Still no?
-Still no. Still even less.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:01.494
But I have a kid now, and so as
long as repeats are happening --

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.263
-They´re going to show it
till I´m old and gray.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-I guarantee it.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I think, like, you know,
five, six years from now,

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.335
I´m going to come into the full
bloom of your early work.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.505
-I´ll finally have a bit of
a mustache in five or six years.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you´ll still be seeing
those episodes.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you -- you were somebody
who liked comics.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Big-time, yeah.
-Worked in a comic book store.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that true?
-I did, yeah.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.682 size:88% position:44%
I worked at a comic shop
called Meltdown Comics.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.717
I used to go to Meltdown Comics
all the time on Sunset.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, those guys
are killing it.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn´t know you
from Disney Channel.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew you as the guy
who sold me comic books.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right,
how the tables have turned.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
Making me feel a little more
in power now.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, but this is sort of,
obviously,

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
a re-imagining
of "Archie" comics.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:41.568
Were you drawn to the idea
of doing it in a different way?

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.604 size:84% position:42%
-At first, if I´m being
completely honest, no.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.506
It seemed a little scary to me.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because when you come
from a comic background,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.843 size:84% position:42%
which I´m sure you get,

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:54.414
you also come from a background
of, like, purity and purism.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Adhering to the source.
-Right, right.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.917
-When you start to see people

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.887
mess with that really nostalgic
property you love,

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.489
it can be quite incendiary.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:06.793 size:88% position:44%
So when I first read it,
I was a little bit wary.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:10.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I-I did my audition
just like Rod Serling

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I went in.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he´s the narrator
in the show.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.033
I read it like Rod Serling.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.835
And I kind of knew from there

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:19.072
it was going to be a little
stranger, a little weirder,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.373
a little more "Twilight Zone."

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.774
And I figured, "Okay, you know,
this could be fun.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:22.876 size:81% position:41%
Let´s give it a shot."

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard you had an argument,
though,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the purity
of Jughead´s dog.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so this is about
the casting of a physical dog.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.286
You had an issue with one
of the show´s creators.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-What was your iss--

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did you think
the dog should be?

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man. Okay.
Now that you´re calling --

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.994
-You´re a very method actor.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.629 size:81% position:41%
You want to work with
the right kind of dog.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I need the right --
I need to live with the dog

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.132
and breathe with the dog.

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:49.536
No, so Jughead´s dog in the
comics is a dog called Hot Dog.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he´s undoubtedly
the worst part of the digests.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hands down,
he´s the scariest thing

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.242
and adds really not too much.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
But for some reason,
I was addicted to the idea

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
of having an English sheepdog
like he is in the comics.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:06.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was originally pitched
as, like, a pit bull.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so you were very upset
with that.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.324
-And, you know, I thought,

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.259 size:88% position:44%
"Okay, well, we got to
try and figure out a way

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.260
to get an English sheepdog."

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.828 size:81% position:41%
So for a week, a week,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:19.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was trying to wear Roberto
down about this.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.667 size:75% position:38%
And we got this dog.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:24.070
And this dog was the worst actor
I have ever --

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The sheepdog?
-The sheepdog, yes.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I grew up with sheepdogs,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they are lovely creatures
who are dumb as rocks.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So dumb. So dumb.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I can´t imagine
any of my dogs

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.380
growing up being able to, like,
hit a mark.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.684
-It barks the whole time.
It didn´t hit its mark.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
It broke fourth wall
consistently.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:42.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was just no good.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.792
-All right. Well, I´m glad
you´re owning up to that.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:46.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I made a mistake.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right, good.
Thank you.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.663
You do something that I love.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:53.333
-Finally.
-You´re very active on Twitter.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.467
-One thing that you love.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.135
-No, no, I love a lot about you.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, um...
-Go on.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But this is great.
So you take advantage of --

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:03.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
People post about you and your
twin brother, Dylan, a lot.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
And your responses to them,
I have to say,

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
are really, really funny,
because you are --

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were these, like,
the news articles?

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.283 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, news articles.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.751
So there´s one, a picture
of your brother that says,

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
"10 child stars
who are completely broke,"

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you wrote
to your brother,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.256 size:88% position:44%
"Did you hear the news?"

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I really like that.
-And he did.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did hear the news.
-He did.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:24.530
This one wrote, "Cole --
I hate wet, sloppy kisses."

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.399
And your response to that was,

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:29.435
"I´m also wearing a plaid
train conductor´s hat,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.272 size:88% position:44%
so why are you trusting
my 10-year-old opinion?"

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Geez.
-This is my favorite, though.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was a look.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a very -- Because you
see these all the time.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.612
They´re, like, click bait.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is "32 child stars
who died shockingly young."

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.985
A photo of you shockingly alive.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.690 size:88% position:44%
-And you wrote, "Dead on
the inside counts, too."

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is excellent.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s excellent.
-Thank you.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But --

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.266
-That was my Twitter peak.

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.501
-No, I think I´m about --

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.670 size:88% position:44%
This, I think, is your
Twitter peak right here.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´m going to --
This is a poem that you wrote.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
You posted a poem you wrote
to your mom.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.076 size:84% position:42%
But instead of showing,
letting people read it,

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.878
I would love for you to read it,
´cause it is --

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.746
You wrote -- And you did write,

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.316 size:75% position:38%
"I was a psycho baby
before it was hip."

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I love you, Mom.
You are the best.

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.586
You´re better than all the rest.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if anyone ever
takes us apart,

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´d repeatedly stab them
in the heart."

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:26.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at -- Now look
at the handwriting!

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.330 size:88% position:44% line:0%
Look how young you were!

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.599 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
That´s fantastic!

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that very in line
with your thinking back then?

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, I just brought
that angst

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.571
all the way into "Riverdale."

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.808
-I´ve been method forever.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, here´s what you need
to know about Jughead.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:47.647
-Congrats on the show.
Really lovely to have you here.

